WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:05.800
Did you ever wonder if certain foods
have a direct effect on your health?

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.760
Well, I’m here to
solve that mystery

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:11.240
since you are
the foods you eat.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.320
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.120
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:20.880
Today we look at the effect of
maternal diets on infant health.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.920
Did you know that you can
treat the cause of infant reflux

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:29.200
with maternal cow’s
milk elimination?

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.360
Here’s our first story.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:36.640
There has been a longstanding problem
among zookeepers of the gorilla.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.440
Latin name: Gorilla, gorilla gorilla.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.920
The problem is that they were
throwing up all the time.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.320
We’ve never seen wild gorillas barfing,

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.440
but it had unfortunately been
accepted as routine by many zoos.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.200
What were they feeding them?

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.080
Well, you know they’re
big strong animals,

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.280
so they made sure to
feed them lots of protein,

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.080
you know, cottage cheese,
meat, eggs, milk.;

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.320
until a zoo in Germany
got this radical idea

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.320
to try giving them their natural diet.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:11.040
And the change following the
alterations to the diet was astonishing.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.000
I mean before, the poor silverback
was regurgitating and vomiting

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.840
during most of the day.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:20.000
But by the third day eating what
they were supposed to eat,

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.440
he and the rest were
all miraculously cured.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:26.560
Even just removing milk from
captive gorilla diets

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.400
led to significant improvement.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.640
Cow’s milk was historically
considered an essential item

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:37.560
in the captive gorilla diet,
but they showed that removal

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:42.120
of milk from the captive gorilla diet
may reduce such undesirable behaviors

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:46.040
and may be a step toward better
approximating their natural diet.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:50.120
I mean giving an animal
milk after weaning?

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.200
Giving an adult animal milk?

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.040
Milk is for babies!

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:59.400
And then giving milk from
a bovine to a primate?

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:02.560
What were these crazy
zookeepers thinking?

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.960
Doesn’t make any sense!

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.600
Reminds me of this landmark study.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:12.560
Eighty-one children presenting with
reflux, gastroesophageal reflux disease,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.760
so they were given drugs,
and two thirds got better,

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:17.480
but 27 kids still did not.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:19.760
So, they tried eliminating cow’s milk

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:27.200
from their diets, and within
one month, all 27 were cured.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:31.120
Symptoms of acid regurgitation,
heartburn, or both, occur

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.480
at least once a week in 10–20 percent
of adults in the western world.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:37.720
And in about up to 25
percent of all infants.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.120
Now it’s normal for babies
to spit up occasionally—

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.920
that’s not what we’re talking about.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:43.880
It can actually get quite serious.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:47.560
Up to a quarter of infants present
with regurgitation severe enough

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.400
for parents to seek medical help,

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:54.160
and it may just be that they’re
sensitive to cow’s milk.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.080
The symptoms of cow’s milk protein
allergy overlap or may coexist

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.960
or complicate GERD or reflux.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:04.280
Even if there’s no formal
dairy allergy per se,

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:07.480
there appears to be some kind
of cow’s milk ‘hypersensitivity’

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:10.760
among many infants and
children with severe reflux.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.640
There are all sorts of
invasive tests you can do,

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:16.800
like stick pH probes down
the poor baby’s throat,

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.520
but probably the most practical test
in routine pediatric practice

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:24.120
is just a trial of a cow’s milk
protein elimination diet

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:28.040
for two to four weeks
in infants with reflux.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:32.240
The gold standard is what’s called an
elimination and re-challenge protocol,

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:36.560
where you see full resolution of
symptoms via a strict elimination,

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.200
followed by recurrence of the symptoms

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.800
on reintroduction of cow’s milk protein.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:45.960
And when you do that, take 200 or
so infants diagnosed with reflux

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:48.640
and then not only put them
on a cow’s milk-free diet,

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.560
but then do the challenge tests.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:55.440
Eighty-five of the 204 infants with
reflux were actually suffering

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:59.560
from a cow’s milk allergy or at least
hypersensitivity or something.

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:02.920
What we think is happening is
that our immune system attacks

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:06.680
the bovine proteins as
understandably foreign,

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.120
triggering an inflammatory response,

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:12.800
which like irritates the nerves
lining your digestive tract,

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:16.360
and that results in abnormalities
in the rhythmic contractions

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:19.520
of the stomach, triggering
the regurgitation.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:22.680
And we’re not just talking
about formula-fed infants.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:28.480
Cow’s milk protein allergy can occur
in exclusively breastfed infants,

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:32.720
as intact cow’s milk proteins can
be secreted in breast milk.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:38.800
If the mom drinks milk or eats
eggs it can get into her baby.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:43.400
Cow’s milk protein and other foreign
proteins can pass into human breast milk.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:47.400
So breast-fed infants with regurgitation
and vomiting may therefore benefit from

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:52.120
a trial of withdrawal of cow’s milk
and eggs from the maternal diet.

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:56.400
And indeed, that is now the
consensus recommendation of both

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:00.040
the North American and European
Society for Pediatric

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:03.080
Gastroenterology, Hepatology,
and Nutrition.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:07.400
Anytime you see reflux, let’s
first try a therapeutic trial

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:11.200
of either a cow’s milk protein–free
formula or, for infants who are breastfed,

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:15.520
a maternal strict cow’s milk
protein elimination diet.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.720
And so, then we can potentially
treat the cause without

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:22.960
using unnecessary medications,
and certainly before you start

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.720
considering performing
any anti-reflux surgery

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.680
on the poor kid.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:28.520
In our next story,

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:33.360
we look at how cow’s milk proteins
can pass through breast milk—

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:36.040
which may explain why
maternal dairy-free diets

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:40.040
are so effective in
treating infant colic.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.280
Colic affects up to 40%
of young infants,

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:48.320
characterized by prolonged periods
of inconsolable crying.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:52.320
The condition is often
dismissed as trivial

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:56.840
by the medical profession,
but should be treated seriously.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:59.600
It can contribute to
postpartum depression,

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:00.680
interfere with breastfeeding,

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:03.720
and even lead to the
death of the infant

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:08.080
at the hands of a parent
from shaken baby syndrome.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:11.680
They’re not just crybabies.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:14.600
Colic is pain.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:17.360
The medical profession has
a scandalous history

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:20.120
not just denying pain
relief to infants,

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:24.240
but routinely performing
surgery on infants

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:28.200
with minimal or no
anesthesia into the 1980’s.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:31.560
One famous case in 1985
was little Jeffrey Lawson,

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:34.280
who underwent open
heart surgery

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:37.320
fully awake and conscious.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:40.680
They just gave him a drug to
paralyze him so he wouldn’t squirm,

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:43.320
but like a horror
movie he couldn’t move

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:45.560
but could feel everything.

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:48.040
This wasn’t some rogue surgeon,

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.760
torturing babies was standard
operating procedure in the 80’s.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:56.280
Not the 1880’s, mind you,
the 1980’s.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:59.960
The liaison between the
American Academy of Pediatrics

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:02.000
and the Society of Anesthesiologists

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.560
commented that the use
of paralyzing agents

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:07.960
was a standard and
time-honored technique.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:12.760
The profession has a history
of infant pain denial.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:16.320
They didn’t think
babies could feel pain.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:19.360
Even today, most physicians
don’t use pain-killers

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:23.040
or even local anesthesia
for circumcisions, for example,

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.360
a procedure so traumatic
the babies show

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:29.520
stronger pain responses to
vaccinations even months later.

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:32.840
The pain of colic,
is thought to be caused

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:36.440
by gastrointestinal discomfort,
like intestinal cramping.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:38.400
In my videos on irritable bowel

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:41.400
and relaxing the colon
before a colonoscopy

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:43.400
I explored the role
of peppermint oil

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:45.240
in reducing intestinal spasms,

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:47.920
so might it help with colic?

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:50.400
A few drops of a peppermint
leaf solution appeared

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:53.800
to cut the number of
colicky episodes in half,

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:56.880
and reduced daily crying from
three hours to two hours,

00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:00.920
working just as well as the
leading over-the-counter drug

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:03.800
for colic called simethicone.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:07.760
The problem is that simethicone
has been shown to have

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:09.480
no benefit for colic,

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:12.640
so saying peppermint
is as good as useless

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:15.480
isn’t exactly a ringing
endorsement.

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:17.280
And the American Academy of Pediatrics

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:21.680
warns about the use of
peppermint oil in infants.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:25.920
One study found an herbal
tea preparation to be helpful,

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:30.960
but parents have been
cautioned not to use them,

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:34.560
not only because tea may interfere
with breastfeeding continuity,

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:37.480
but the lack of adequate
industry regulation.

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:42.920
For example, star anise tea
is commonly used for colic.

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:46.000
Chinese star anise is regarded
as safe and nontoxic,

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.840
but Japanese star
anise is poisonous.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:53.480
They look identical,
but Japanese star anise

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:55.280
contains a potent neurotoxin,

00:08:55.280 --> 00:09:00.800
and it’s been found contaminating
star anise tea in the U.S.,

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:04.040
and so we shouldn’t
give it to kids.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:05.920
There’s even a
report of toxicity

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:09.440
from a supposed homeopathic
dose of belladonna,

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.040
also known as
deadly nightshade,

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:14.000
that evidently wasn’t homeopathic
enough, and then another.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:18.920
Just because it’s homeopathic doesn’t
necessarily mean it’s safe.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:22.240
It’s no better when doctors
prescribe it though.

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:26.480
The drugs used for colic are
made from belladonna too.

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:31.240
The drugs may work,
but should not be used

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:34.320
because of their
serious side effects.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:37.600
What about just good
old fashioned burping?

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:40.440
Burping after feeding is,
after all, commonly advised

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:42.880
by pediatricians, nurses
and parenting websites

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:46.280
to promote expulsion of gases that
accumulate during feeding

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:49.760
with the aim of decreasing
discomfort and crying episodes,

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:53.760
but scientific evidence for the
efficacy of burping is lacking,

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:57.120
until this 2014 randomized
controlled trial

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:00.000
for the prevention of colic
and regurgitation,

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.000
also known as spitting up,
in healthy infants.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.000
So what did they find?

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:11.440
Useless for colic, and made
the regurgitation worse.

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:17.480
Burped babies spit up twice
as many times as unburped babies!

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:21.000
So what’s an
effective treatment?

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:24.880
The elimination of
cow’s milk protein,

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:28.240
thinking colic may be some
sort of allergic response.

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:32.320
Decades ago it was shown
that infants fed cow’s milk

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:35.040
developed antibody responses
to the bovine proteins,

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:37.320
which may explain why
colic can improve

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.400
after changing from a
cow’s milk formula

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:42.320
to either a hypoallergenic
hydrolyzed protein formula

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.240
or a soy-based formula.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:46.560
Now, breast fed infants
have similar rates

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:49.240
of colic as formula
fed infants,

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:54.400
but that might be because breast
milk from milk drinking mothers

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:56.640
contains cow's milk proteins.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:59.880
We know cow’s milk proteins
can pass through breast milk

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:02.080
and cause certain serious
allergic reactions,

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:04.600
but what about colic?

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.640
Based on studies of
formula fed infants,

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:09.760
colic was already a well-known
symptom of intolerance

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:12.440
to cow’s-milk protein
back in the 70’s,

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:15.320
so thinking colic in
breast-fed infants

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.920
may be caused by cow’s-milk
proteins transmitted

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:20.560
from mother to infant
via breast milk,

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:23.960
they tried a dairy-free diet
for breast-feeding mothers

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:26.520
whose infants had colic.

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:31.160
Of 19 infants, the colic
disappeared promptly from 13,

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:33.080
and in 12 of those 13
they were able to show

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.160
that they could bring
back the colic by

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:38.080
challenging the mothers
with a little dairy.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:40.560
For example, baby boy
develops colic

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:43.400
that almost completely
disappears within a day

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:45.680
of mom eliminating cow’s milk,

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:49.280
and then promptly comes back
when mom went back on dairy.

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:52.240
The researches conclude that
the treatment for infantile colic

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:56.300
in breast-fed infants is a diet
free of cow’s milk for the mother,

00:11:56.300 --> 00:12:01.360
a recommendation that
continues to this day.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:02.120
Finally today,

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:05.080
we look at how spirulina
supplements with toxins

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:10.400
from blue-green algae raise
safety concerns for nursing mothers.

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:15.640
On his first day of life an infant
is hospitalized with seizures.

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:18.960
The researchers concluded that his
mother's daily spirulina use

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:24.600
starting in the 4th month of
pregnancy was likely to blame.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:27.840
I've talked previously about
the liver and nerve toxins

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:30.520
present in many spirulina supplements,

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:32.440
but the supplement companies
swear up and down

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:37.480
that spirulina doesn't produce
these toxins and they may be right.

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:39.680
But if spirulina doesn't produce toxins,

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:42.160
how was it that toxins have
been repeatedly been found

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:44.360
in spirulina supplements?

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:50.520
It appears to be contamination of spirulina
with toxin-producing blue-green algae.

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:56.200
So for example if you look at the new U.S.
Pharmacopeia safety evaluation of spirulina,

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:58.720
they conclude that the available
evidence does not indicate

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:01.640
a serious risk or other
public health concern

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:05.840
when spirulina is properly
identified, formulated, and used.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:07.600
Ah, but that's the catch!

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:09.920
You collect spirulina
in some open lake

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:13.280
and you have no idea what other
algae are going to crop up.

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:16.640
The researchers report
all sorts of adverse reactions

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:19.360
in people taking
spirulina products,

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:24.600
but they attribute these issues to
non-spirulina algae toxin contaminants

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:26.920
within spirulina supplements

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:30.640
known to be toxic to the liver
and cancer-causing.

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:34.560
So unless there's third-party
testing of each batch,

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:38.000
which no company could
presumably afford to do,

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:43.200
I continue to encourage people
to avoid spirulina products.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:45.400
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:48.840
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:51.480
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:55.720
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:59.640
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

